 ## Usage
 
 ```sh
-aread              # render recent turns of this directory's latest session, open in browser
-aread list         # table of recent sessions across both CLIs
+aread                              # render this directory's latest session
+aread list                         # table of recent sessions across all harnesses
+agent-read list --json             # machine-readable session index
+agent-read transcript --session ID # normalized turns for one session as JSON
 ```
 
 `aread` scopes to the session whose working directory is the current directory
 and falls back to the newest session anywhere. From inside a Claude Code
 session, type `! aread` to pop the turn you're looking at into a readable page.
 
+The table form of `agent-read list` shows the newest 20 sessions by default.
+`--limit N` sets a positive bound, and `--limit 0` means all. JSON mode defaults to all
+sessions so local consumers do not silently lose older history.
+
+`agent-read list --json` includes each session's harness, ID, path, cwd, optional
+name, and activity time. `agent-read transcript --session ID` emits normalized prompts
+and assistant blocks with timestamps, provider, and model. Both JSON outputs are private
+and intended for local tools; redirect them only to private storage.
+
